# SABOTAGE: UXD-07 / A6 — samen_postmark is the first ESP adapter to consume the SHARED
# cross-family kit `Samen.AdapterConformanceCase` (T188) instead of the ESP-only
# `Samen.Delivery.ProviderConformanceCase` macro harness. An adopted kit that would pass a
# broken adapter has adopted nothing, so this patch widens SamenPostmark.Provider's
# redaction allowlist to admit the two PII-bearing Postmark bounce keys (`Email`, the
# bounced recipient address, and `FromName`, the sender display name). redact_payload/1
# then persists plaintext PII verbatim — the exact leak ADR-038 §4.5(d) forbids. The named
# red is the redaction test in samen_postmark/test/conformance_test.exs, whose assertion is
# `Samen.AdapterConformanceCase.assert_redaction!/3` in samen_core: if it does not flip, the
# kit's delivery-shaped assertions are not actually running against the adapter. The other
# seven conformance tests stay GREEN under this patch, proving the flip is surgical and the
# suite is not blanket-failing.
# APP: samen_postmark
# TEST_FILES: test/conformance_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: redact_payload/1 strips every known-PII fixture string
diff --git a/samen_postmark/lib/samen_postmark/provider.ex b/samen_postmark/lib/samen_postmark/provider.ex
index c7540b7..90c836e 100644
--- a/samen_postmark/lib/samen_postmark/provider.ex
+++ b/samen_postmark/lib/samen_postmark/provider.ex
@@ -69,10 +69,18 @@ defmodule SamenPostmark.Provider do
   # safe merely because the key name is safe. `Metadata` — and every other
   # nested map/list (`Headers`, `Attachments`, …) — is dropped WHOLESALE,
   # never selectively descended into.
+  # SABOTAGE (UXD-07 / A6): the redaction allowlist is widened to admit the two
+  # PII-bearing Postmark bounce keys — `Email` (the bounced recipient address) and
+  # `FromName` (the sender's display name). redact_payload/1 then persists plaintext
+  # PII verbatim, exactly the leak ADR-038 §4.5(d) exists to forbid. MUST FLIP the
+  # redaction test in samen_postmark/test/conformance_test.exs, which is
+  # Samen.AdapterConformanceCase.assert_redaction!/3 — the delivery-shaped assertion
+  # the cross-family kit gained when samen_postmark adopted it. If that test still
+  # passes, the adopted kit's assertions are not actually running.
   @safe_keys ~w(
     RecordType ID Type TypeCode Name Tag MessageID ServerID Description
     Details BouncedAt DeliveredAt ReceivedAt SentAt Inactive CanActivate
-    DumpAvailable
+    DumpAvailable Email FromName
   )
 
   @impl true
